## C. Self-measurement claims (R-J2: do not measure)

_None yet._

**Standing note:** resource dashboards, CPU/RAM breakdowns, and per-job error
inventories are **not** design evidence. A component's resource cost is not a
measure of whether its design works.

## D. Excluded

Per user scope. **Record the count and the rule; never open an excluded file,
summarize it, or infer its contents.** If one looks misclassified, record that
here and move on.

Exclusion is a standing scope instruction, not progress — a restart of the read
does not reopen excluded files.

## E. Workspace integrity

_Record any case where the workspace's own progress record was found wrong._

A progress record that can be silently falsified will eventually produce an arena
claiming conclusions from files nobody read. Treat any unexpected drop in the read
count as this until proven otherwise, and say so in the run report rather than
silently re-marking.

